From 38559fcd1c518a33055ef0a2cf7c04b57bfa9215 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bui duc phuc <phucduc.bui@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:38:13 +0700
Subject: ASoC: amd: vangogh: Fix acp5x_dma_close() being skipped on rollback
Git-commit: 38559fcd1c518a33055ef0a2cf7c04b57bfa9215
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc1
References: git-fixes

snd_pcm_hw_constraint_integer() may return 1, which is then returned
from acp5x_dma_open(). ASoC only marks the component as opened
when .open() returns 0, so .close() can be skipped on rollback.

Return 0 explicitly on success.

Fixes: cab396d8b22c ("ASoC: amd: add ACP5x pcm dma driver ops")
Signed-off-by: bui duc phuc <phucduc.bui@gmail.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261008103831.542533-7-phucduc.bui@gmail.com
Signed-off-by: Mark Brown <broonie@kernel.org>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 sound/soc/amd/vangogh/acp5x-pcm-dma.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/amd/vangogh/acp5x-pcm-dma.c b/sound/soc/amd/vangogh/acp5x-pcm-dma.c
index 831e30e9b042..33d59d992ee0 100644
--- a/sound/soc/amd/vangogh/acp5x-pcm-dma.c
+++ b/sound/soc/amd/vangogh/acp5x-pcm-dma.c
@@ -231,7 +231,7 @@ static int acp5x_dma_open(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 	}
 	i2s_data->acp5x_base = adata->acp5x_base;
 	runtime->private_data = i2s_data;
-	return ret;
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static int acp5x_dma_hw_params(struct snd_soc_component *component,
-- 
